WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:08.600
On September 20th, Kiribati became the
seventh country to cut off diplomatic

00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:13.710
relations with Taiwan since president
Tsai's election. Four days prior, the

00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:17.460
Solomon Islands did the same. These
decisions to normalize relations with

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:21.420
Beijing by Taiwan's largest Pacific
partners may convince Taipei's three

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:26.099
remaining Pacific allies to reconsider
their positions. Poaching Taiwan's

00:00:26.099 --> 00:00:29.699
allies helps China isolate the island,
which could aid in its so-called

00:00:29.699 --> 00:00:34.649
reunification efforts. China leverages
trade and promises future investment to

00:00:34.649 --> 00:00:38.640
convince countries to switch their
recognition. China was the Solomon Islands

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:41.790
biggest trade partner, and allegedly
promised them five hundred million

00:00:41.790 --> 00:00:46.170
dollars in financial aid. China also
promised Kiribati full funding for its

00:00:46.170 --> 00:00:49.710
airplanes and commercial ferries. Taiwan
is at risk of losing more of their

00:00:49.710 --> 00:00:52.949
partners because they just can't compete
with Chinese aid and trade.

00:00:52.949 --> 00:00:56.670
Moreover, the United States is reducing
aid to some of Taiwan's remaining allies.

00:00:56.670 --> 00:01:00.090
Congress and the White House are
considering a strategy that would punish

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:03.750
countries for abandoning Taiwan, but it
would be more effective to offer

00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:06.860
benefits to those that decided to
support Taipei.

00:01:07.480 --> 00:01:11.520
Do you think the United States should
help Taiwan keep its allies? Let us know

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:15.479
in our poll. Also, let us know what other
topics you'd like our scholars to cover

00:01:15.479 --> 00:01:20.490
in 60 seconds, and be sure to like and
subscribe for more research and videos

00:01:20.490 --> 00:01:23.360
from AEI.

